{"id":"gpt2-residual-projection-init","t":"GPT-2 initialisation plan with scaled residual projections","tags":["Language Models","Training","Neural Networks"],"d":"Easy","rt":"python","fn":"init_plan","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"GPT-2 initialises weights from $\\mathcal N(0, 0.02^2)$, except the projections that write into the residual stream, which are scaled by $1/\\sqrt{2L}$ for $L$ layers.\n\nWrite `init_plan(names, n_layer, base=0.02)` that maps parameter names to an initialisation, checking rules in this order:\n\n1. A name whose last two dot-separated parts are a LayerNorm (`ln_1`, `ln_2`, `ln_f`) followed by `weight` → `[\"const\", 1.0]`; followed by `bias` → `[\"const\", 0.0]`.\n2. Any other name ending in `.bias` → `[\"const\", 0.0]`.\n3. A name ending in `attn.c_proj.weight` or `mlp.c_proj.weight` → `[\"normal\", base / sqrt(2 * n_layer)]`.\n4. Any other name ending in `weight` → `[\"normal\", base]`.\n5. Anything else raises `ValueError`.\n\nReturn a dict from name to that two-element list.","starter":"def init_plan(names, n_layer, base=0.02):\n    \"\"\"Map parameter names to [\"normal\", std] or [\"const\", value].\"\"\"\n    return {n: [\"normal\", base] for n in names}\n","hints":["Check LayerNorm names before the generic bias and weight rules, because ln_1.weight also ends in \"weight\".","Each block has two residual writes (attention and MLP), which is where the 2 in sqrt(2L) comes from."],"sol":"import math\n\ndef init_plan(names, n_layer, base=0.02):\n    plan = {}\n    for n in names:\n        parts = n.split(\".\")\n        if len(parts) >= 2 and parts[-2] in (\"ln_1\", \"ln_2\", \"ln_f\") and parts[-1] in (\"weight\", \"bias\"):\n            plan[n] = [\"const\", 1.0 if parts[-1] == \"weight\" else 0.0]\n        elif n.endswith(\".bias\"):\n            plan[n] = [\"const\", 0.0]\n        elif n.endswith(\"attn.c_proj.weight\") or n.endswith(\"mlp.c_proj.weight\"):\n            plan[n] = [\"normal\", base / math.sqrt(2 * n_layer)]\n        elif n.endswith(\"weight\"):\n            plan[n] = [\"normal\", base]\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"no rule for {n}\")\n    return plan\n","ex_md":"## Why scale the residual projections\nEach block adds its output to the residual stream. With $2L$ independent additions of variance $\\sigma^2$, the stream's variance grows like $2L\\sigma^2$. Scaling those projections by $1/\\sqrt{2L}$ keeps the total roughly constant at initialisation, so deep models start with activations and gradients of the same size as shallow ones.\n\n## What is left at the defaults\nEmbeddings and the input-side projections use 0.02. LayerNorm starts as the identity (scale 1, shift 0) and biases at zero, so the network's first forward pass is driven only by the random projections.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- How does pre-LayerNorm interact with residual growth compared with post-LayerNorm?\n- What do later schemes such as scaled embedding multipliers or μP change about this?","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"['wte.weight', 'wpe.weight', 'h.0.ln_1.weight', 'h.0.ln_1.bias', 'h.0.attn.c_attn.weight', 'h.0.attn.c_attn.bias', 'h.0.attn.c_proj.weight', 'h.0.attn.c_proj.bias', 'h.0.ln_2.weight', 'h.0.ln_2.bias', 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.weight', 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.bias', 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.weight', 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.bias', 'ln_f.weight', 'ln_f.bias']\n1","out":"{'wte.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'wpe.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'h.0.ln_1.weight': ['const', 1.0], 'h.0.ln_1.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.attn.c_attn.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'h.0.attn.c_attn.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.attn.c_proj.weight': ['normal', 0.014142135623730949], 'h.0.attn.c_proj.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.ln_2.weight': ['const', 1.0], 'h.0.ln_2.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.weight': ['normal', 0.014142135623730949], 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'ln_f.weight': ['const', 1.0], 'ln_f.bi …"},{"in":"['wte.weight', 'wpe.weight', 'h.0.ln_1.weight', 'h.0.ln_1.bias', 'h.0.attn.c_attn.weight', 'h.0.attn.c_attn.bias', 'h.0.attn.c_proj.weight', 'h.0.attn.c_proj.bias', 'h.0.ln_2.weight', 'h.0.ln_2.bias', 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.weight', 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.bias', 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.weight', 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.bias', 'h.1.ln_1.weight', 'h.1.ln_1.bias', 'h.1.attn.c_attn.weight', 'h.1.attn.c_attn.bias', 'h.1.attn.c_proj.weight', 'h.1.attn.c_proj.bias', 'h.1.ln_2.weight', 'h.1.ln_2.bias', 'h.1.mlp.c_fc.weight', 'h.1.mlp.c_fc.bias', 'h.1.mlp.c_proj.weight', 'h.1.mlp.c_proj.bias', 'h.2.ln_1.weight', 'h.2.ln_1.bias', 'h.2.at …\n12","out":"{'wte.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'wpe.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'h.0.ln_1.weight': ['const', 1.0], 'h.0.ln_1.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.attn.c_attn.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'h.0.attn.c_attn.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.attn.c_proj.weight': ['normal', 0.004082482904638631], 'h.0.attn.c_proj.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.ln_2.weight': ['const', 1.0], 'h.0.ln_2.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.weight': ['normal', 0.02], 'h.0.mlp.c_fc.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.weight': ['normal', 0.004082482904638631], 'h.0.mlp.c_proj.bias': ['const', 0.0], 'h.1.ln_1.weight': ['const', 1.0], 'h.1 …"}],"lessons":[],"related":[],"ntests":5,"tj":"[{\"a\": [[\"wte.weight\", \"wpe.weight\", \"h.0.ln_1.weight\", \"h.0.ln_1.bias\", \"h.0.attn.c_attn.weight\", \"h.0.attn.c_attn.bias\", \"h.0.attn.c_proj.weight\", \"h.0.attn.c_proj.bias\", \"h.0.ln_2.weight\", \"h.0.ln_2.bias\", \"h.0.mlp.c_fc.weight\", \"h.0.mlp.c_fc.bias\", \"h.0.mlp.c_proj.weight\", \"h.0.mlp.c_proj.bias\", \"ln_f.weight\", \"ln_f.bias\"], 1], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"wte.weight\", [\"normal\", 0.02]], [\"wpe.weight\", [\"normal\", 0.02]], [\"h.0.ln_1.weight\", [\"const\", 1.0]], [\"h.0.ln_1.bias\", [\"const\", 0.0]], [\"h.0.attn.c_attn.weight\", [\"normal\", 0.02]], [\"h.0.attn.c_attn.bias\", [\"const\", 0.0]], [\"h.0.attn.c_proj.weight\", [\"normal\", 0.014142135623730949]], [\"h.0.attn.c_proj.bias\", [\"const\", 0.0]], [\"h.0.ln_2.weight\", [\"c